---
source: crates/dyno-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "help(&[\"--help\"])"
---
Predicts how much memory an HTML5 game in an iframe will use on an iPhone, from its build.

Each command but mcp writes one canonical JSON result to stdout, or to --out. A short summary for people goes to stderr. It has no stable format, so do not parse it.

Usage: dyno <COMMAND>

Commands:
  check    [phase 1] Check a build folder, a launch URL, or every game in a games file
  compare  [phase 1] Diff two result files from `dyno check`
  doctor   [phase 2] Check that this Mac can run the game on an iPhone
  mcp      [phase 3] Serve check, compare and read_result to an MCP client on stdin and stdout
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Exit codes:
  0   pass, or warn
  1   fail: a budget or rule fails
  2   incomplete: a required measure is missing, or a budget or rule could not be checked
  3   invalid: a required measure or an input result failed its own check
  64  usage or config error
  70  internal or I/O error
